  "nb-drug-plan": {
    "name": "New Brunswick Drug Plan",
    "keys": [
      "nb-drug-plan",
      "nb drug plan",
      "new brunswick drug plan"
    ],
    "text": "How to apply:\n  1. Get an active New Brunswick Medicare card if you do not have one. New residents must do this first.\n  2. Fill in the New Brunswick Drug Plan Application Form. Give spouse details even if your spouse is not applying.\n  3. If you have private coverage, add the Supporting Application Form Other Drug Coverage for each applicant.\n  4. Add a letter from your private plan saying the maximum is reached or the drug is not listed.\n  5. Mail the forms to PO Box 690, Moncton, NB E1C 8M7, or fax them to [phone — see the guide].\nWhat you need:\n  - New Brunswick Drug Plan Application Form (one per family)\n  - Supporting Application Form Other Drug Coverage (one per applicant, if you have other coverage)\n  - Letter from each private plan, if you have other coverage\n  - Special authorization request from your health care provider, if the drug needs one\nPractical tips:\n  - From November 1, 2026, the lowest premium is [amount — see the guide] a month per adult, or [amount — see the guide] a year.\n  - From November 1, 2026, the highest premium is [amount — see the guide] a month per adult, or [amount — see the guide] a year.\n  - You also pay [percentage — see the guide] of each prescription, up to [amount — see the guide] in the lowest band and [amount — see the guide] in the highest.\n  - The Drug Plan pays last. It does not coordinate benefits with other plans.\n  - It will not consider requests where your private plan's own rules for the condition are not met.\n  - If you do not file a tax return, you are charged the maximum annual premium. File one each year.\n  - Call the Drug Plan to check that a drug is on the Formulary.\nHow long it takes (verified — you may state this): Monday to Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.",
    "phone": "1-800-332-3692"
  },
  "nb-hearing-aid-program": {
    "name": "Health Services Hearing Aid Program",
    "keys": [
      "nb-hearing-aid-program",
      "nb hearing aid program",
      "health services hearing aid program"
    ],
    "text": "How to apply:\n  1. Get a certified audiologist's report and a copy of your audiogram.\n  2. Get 1 estimate from a licensed provider registered with the NB Hearing Aid Society, on a Health Services invoice.\n  3. Send your request to the Health Services Program for prior approval.\n  4. Buy from a New Brunswick supplier unless the item is not available in the province.\nWhat you need:\n  - Certified audiologist's report with specifications\n  - Copy of the audiogram\n  - 1 estimate on a Health Services invoice\n  - Serial number\n  - Physician's prescription, when testing was done outside a hospital (first request only)\n  - Warranty details and expiry date\nPractical tips:\n  - Replacement is not automatic after 5 years. You must show the need.\n  - Not covered: cochlear implants, personal FM systems, BAHA and CIC aids, and hearing tests.\n  - Charger repairs, T-coil and directional microphone options are not covered either."
  },
