    "text": "How to apply:\n  1. Get the application from a Motor Registration office or the website.\n  2. Ask a doctor or nurse practitioner to fill it out the first time.\n  3. Email it, fax it, or mail or drop it at any Motor Registration Office.\n  4. Receive the permit by mail, or ask to pick it up at an office.\nWhat you need:\n  - Accessible Parking Permit Application completed by a doctor or nurse practitioner.\nPractical tips:\n  - A temporary permit is valid for six months and a permanent one for five years; the Registrar decides the length.\n  - Processing takes [age limit — see the guide] business days, and may change with volume.\n  - Renew a permanent permit online at MyGovNL; no new doctor visit is needed.\n  - A temporary permit cannot be renewed; send a new application.\n  - Email accessparkingpermits@gov.nl.ca or fax [phone — see the guide].",
