    "text": "How to apply:\n  1. Open the Financial Supports page and get the children's application form.\n  2. Fill in the form completely.\n  3. Attach the documents the form asks for.\n  4. Send it in before the deadline for your program.\n  5. Wait for the City to tell you the result.\nWhat you need:\n  - Proof of residency showing your name and address, such as a utility bill or driver's license\n  - Proof of income from all sources, such as a Canada Revenue Agency Notice of Assessment for the previous year\n  - A Canada Child Tax Benefit Notice is another example of income proof\nPractical tips:\n  - Deadlines are Feb 1 for spring camp, Mar 1 for preschool and after school care, and Mar 17 for summer camp.\n  - A deadline that falls on a weekend moves to the next Monday.\n  - The page asks you to allow [age limit — see the guide] business days for a reply.\n  - The page's example is from 2022 (2021 income), so the tax year to use now is not stated there.\n  - For Notice of Assessment, call [phone — see the guide]; for Child Tax Benefit Notice, call [phone — see the guide].\nHow long it takes (verified — you may state this): [age limit — see the guide] business days for a reply",
