    "text": "How to apply:\n  1. Call Income Support and ask which work incentives apply to you.\n  2. Report your employment earnings every month.\n  3. Ask about childcare help, which comes from Education (licensed) or Income Support (private).\nWhat you need:\n  - The page does not list documents.\nPractical tips:\n  - Job Start benefit is [amount — see the guide] up to two times per year for new jobs.\n  - After the first 60 days, the first [amount — see the guide] a month you earn is not deducted from your Income Support benefits.\n  - Single parents may also get an Earned Income Supplement.\n  - Continuation Bonuses are [amount — see the guide] at 6 months, [amount — see the guide] at 12 months and [amount — see the guide] at 24 months of continuous work.\n  - Up to [amount — see the guide] Employment Stability Assistance may help in a financial emergency that could stop you working.\n  - Jobs, Growth and Rural Development can help with work expenses: [phone — see the guide] or employmentprograms@gov.nl.ca.",
